DESCRIPTION:
  Config-file + runtime-state gated command injection. The server reads
  exec_mode and exec_secret from a config file. A /exec/init?token= endpoint
  must be called first with the correct secret to create a flag file
  (EXEC_INIT_FLAG). The main /exec guard checks exec_cfg.enabled &&
  exec_initialized() where exec_initialized() does stat(EXEC_INIT_FLAG).
  Because mini_httpd forks per-request, the "initialized" state is persisted
  via a flag file rather than a global. The cmd parameter flows directly to
  system() (I1) after a pipe-filter (S2, bypass with semicolon).

CONFIG_GATE (C3 -- config file + runtime state):
  mechanism:  Key=value config file parsed by read_exec_config() into
              exec_cfg {enabled, secret}. A /exec/init?token= request
              validates token against exec_cfg.secret and creates flag file
              EXEC_INIT_FLAG. exec_initialized() checks stat(EXEC_INIT_FLAG).
  check:      `if ( exec_cfg.enabled && exec_initialized() && strncmp(path,"/exec",5)==0 ... )`
  complexity: requires modelling both fopen->fgets->sscanf data flow AND
              inter-request state (flag file existence check)

INPUT_FLOW (I1 -- direct):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  ->  global `query`
  path:       handle_exec() sets cmd = query + 4; system(cmd)
  transforms: none

SANITIZATION (S2 -- pipe blocked, bypass with semicolon):
  mechanism:  strchr(cmd, '|') != NULL -> reject 403
  bypass:     use ';' for command chaining

SINK:        system(cmd) in handle_exec() (mini_httpd.c, injected before do_file)

